Limine v12.9.3 (the boot loader, since 0.13)
=============================================================================

What:     the unmodified binary package limine-binary.tar.xz of release
          v12.9.3, https://github.com/Limine-Bootloader/Limine
          (SHA-256 e02a473c6dc6df25159697f94930272397f21fd86e5d4eeee61bba72c95ec8d2;
          its GPG signature was verified once, in 0.13 stage 1, against the
          key 05D2 9860 D0A0 668A AEFB 9D69 1F3C 021B ECA2 3821).
How:      a separate boot tool (AGENTS.md section 11, item 5). It is fetched
          at build time by scripts/install-deps.sh, never kept in this
          repository. Every Madire OS ISO ships its BIOS files
          (/boot/limine/limine-bios.sys, /boot/limine/limine-bios-cd.bin and
          the boot sectors that "limine bios-install" writes), its licence
          (/boot/limine/LICENSE) and its third-party notices
          (/boot/limine/3RDPARTY.md). Only its host tool is built, from the
          package's own limine.c, and it is not shipped.
Licence:  BSD-2-Clause (the package's LICENSE, identical to COPYING at the
          tag v12.9.3), reproduced below.

Limine's binaries also contain code from other projects, under their own
licences: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception (cc-runtime), Apache-2.0 (PCG),
MIT (the Multiboot 2 header, QOI, LAI, stb_image), BSD-2-Clause (Flanterm,
libfdt), 0BSD (pdgzip, the freestanding C headers, the Limine protocol
header) and CC0-1.0 (BLAKE2, OSDev Wiki code); the stage-1 decoder of the
BIOS boot sectors is a modified version of the Micro LZMA decoder, whose
original is under CC-BY-3.0 (Limine's modifications are BSD-2-Clause). The
copyright notices and the full licence texts of all of them are in Limine's
3RDPARTY.md, which goes with the binaries in every ISO
(/boot/limine/3RDPARTY.md, SHA-256
292659d622cddafe3ddab7506e9c501d4a2f7af395090767d9357203e30029a8, the file of
the tag v12.9.3; upstream:
https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine/blob/v12.9.3/3RDPARTY.md).

Known item (accepted in 0.13, decision D2): the cursor-position code in
Limine's common/drivers/vga_textmode.c, built into the BIOS binaries, comes
from the OSDev Wiki before its 2011 relicensing to CC0, and Limine's own
3RDPARTY.md says it was "never confirmed to have been opted into CC0". Its
licence is therefore unconfirmed. See docs/evaluations/limine.md.

